  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-22: \"the term AGIE has snuck thru in the UI in different parts where it doesnt belong. Agie is a machine, not a feature or operation.. it supports Klartext and iso wire edm.\"\n\nWhat happens:\n- Text that the user sees names Agie as if it were a feature, a post type or an operation rule. The machine name leaks into the product surface.\n- The code names it the same way: `crates/app/src/posting_agie.rs`, `operation/agie_profile.rs` and `crates/post/src/agie/`.\n\nWhere it shows on `origin/main` at 054c1e24b (found by text search; the screens were not opened):\n- `crates/app/src/posting.rs:62`: the wire post list holds the entry \"Agie native wire EDM\" (`posting_agie.rs:17`). It sits beside the neutral entries \"Generic ISO Wire EDM\" and \"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\".\n- `assets/posts/agie-native.cps`: the post description reads \"Agie native wire EDM: ...\", and its parameter group reads \"Agie technology\".\n- `crates/app/src/operation/agie_profile.rs` and `posting_agie.rs`: about 40 refusal messages start with \"Agie requires ...\" or \"Agie supports ...\". The user reads them in the post dialog. `AGIE_QN2` shows as a machine condition name.\n- `crates/app/src/script/report.rs`, `posting_files.rs`, `posting_mounts.rs` and `posting_per_op.rs` also name Agie.\n\nExpected:\n- Agie is a machine. It belongs in the machine library: the machine file, its model name and its description.\n- What the machine understands is a dialect of wire EDM output: Klartext and ISO. A post, a refusal or a parameter names the dialect or the capability. It does not name the machine.\n- A refusal says what is wrong with the program (\"The job needs a closed convex punch\"), not which machine brand dislikes it.\n\nDo not change:\n- The posted output. Golden files stay equal.\n- The machine file name and the model name `AGIECUT CLASSIC 2S` in the machine library. They are true statements about the machine.\n- The attribution in `assets/ui/LICENSES.md`.\n\nCheck before the work:\n- A project file can store the post name \"Agie native wire EDM\". A rename must keep old project files readable (alias or migration), or the issue records the break.\n- Open PRs in the Agie stack (#3219, #2999, #2993 and the PRs below them) add more text of this kind. The fix must land in a way that those PRs can take.\n- The post name can reach the command line, the MCP tools and the project file. Check each.\n\nDone means:\n- A search of `crates/ui` and of each user-visible string in `crates/app` finds the word Agie only in the machine library entry.\n- The post list names the dialect (Klartext, ISO), not the machine.\n- A test pins the post list and the refusal text without the word Agie.\n- Posted output is unchanged (golden tests green).\n\nRefs #2951.\n",
